On-device AI means that the AI system runs directly on your device, like a smartphone or computer, instead of sending data to the cloud (a server on the internet). This means the AI processes information locally, which makes it faster and more secure. For example, when you use a camera on your phone, the AI might instantly recognize faces or objects, without needing to send all the data to a server. However, this AI is often pre-installed on the device, and it might need updates to improve its performance.

